>> title: Chicken Shawarma
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: chicken, middle eastern, oven, shawarma spice, yogurt marinade
>> counters: Shawarma Counter, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: chicken shawarma, shawarma djaj, shish shawarma, shwarma, shawerma, chawarma, chicken doner, chicken döner, chicken gyro, shaved chicken
>> pairs-with: shawarma-spice, white-sauce, pita-bread, toum
>> servings: 6
>> time: 14 hr
>> slack: narrow — the fifteen minutes at 450°F is blackening the crown, and it does not stop there once the outside has gone

>> step: coat every piece, marinate 12 hr
Coat @boneless chicken thighs{3%lb}(1.4 kg; skin on, opened out flat) piece by piece with @shawarma spice{3%Tbs}(one batch), @whole-milk yogurt{1/2%cup}(120 g), @lemon juice{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @garlic{6%cloves}(crushed), @olive oil{3%Tbs}(45 mL) and @kosher salt{2%tsp}, then cover and ~marinate{12%hr} in the fridge.

>> step: stack and press into the tin
Stack @&(~1)marinated chicken{} flat in a #loaf tin{}, pressing each piece hard onto the last so there is no air between them, and cap it with @lamb fat{2%oz}(60 g; or two extra skins) and @yellow onion{1%large}(in thick slices).

>> step: roast 325°F 1 1/4 hr, then 450°F 15 min
Roast @&(~1)stack{} in the #oven{} at 325°F (160°C) ~roast{1 1/4%hr}, until a skewer meets no resistance, then take it to 450°F (230°C) for ~roast{15%min} to blacken the crown.

>> step: rest 20 min, shave off the block
Rest @&(~1)roasted stack{} ~rest{20%min}, turn it out of the tin, and shave it down the sides in thin sheets with a long knife, the way it comes off the cone.

>> step: crisp in the pan 2 min
Crisp @&(~1)shavings{} in a very hot #skillet{} in @rendered fat{1%Tbs}(from the tin) ~sear{2%min}, tossing once, until the edges catch and go brittle.
